<body class="bolt-os">

<a href="#main" class="skip-link">Skip to main content</a>

<site-header></site-header>

<main class="atmos" data-screen-label="tools" id="main">
  <section>
    <div class="page-wrap">
      <div class="tools-hero">
        <div class="section-eyebrow"><span class="num">Tools</span> Free · No login</div>
        <h1>Play with the argument.</h1>
        <p class="lede">The essays make a case about the creator economy. These let you test it: a year as a creator, the real cost of an upload schedule, three questions to ask before you sign a deal.</p>
        <p class="lede">Everything runs in your browser. Nothing to install, nothing to hand over.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="tools-count">
        <span class="l">All tools</span>
        <span class="n">{{ collections.tools.length }} and counting</span>
      </div>

      <div class="tool-grid">
        {%- for tool in collections.tools %}
        <a class="tool-card" href="{{ tool.data.url }}">
          <span class="kind">{{ tool.data.kind }}</span>
          <h3>{{ tool.data.title }}</h3>
          <p class="tagline">{{ tool.data.tagline }}</p>
          <div class="desc">{{ tool.templateContent | safe }}</div>
          <div class="foot">
            <span class="meta">{{ tool.data.time }}</span>
            <span class="go">{{ tool.data.cta }} →</span>
          </div>
        </a>
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>

      <div class="tools-why">
        <div class="section-eyebrow">Why these exist</div>
        <h2>A spreadsheet never changed anyone's mind.</h2>
        <p>Most of what I write comes down to one claim: the platforms reward things they don't say they reward, and the bill lands on the people making the content. A game or a calculator makes that felt in ten minutes in a way an essay can't.</p>
        <p>New ones show up here as I build them. If you want to know when, <a href="https://jasonnellis.substack.com/subscribe" target="_blank" rel="noopener">The Long Yes</a> is where I say so. If you want one built for your team or your event, <a href="/contact">get in touch</a>.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- SUBSTACK SUBSCRIBE BANNER -->
      <div class="subscribe-banner" style="margin-top: 56px">
        <div class="sub-content">
          <span class="sub-eyebrow">Newsletter</span>
          <p class="sub-headline">Get <em>The Long Yes</em> in your inbox.</p>
          <p class="sub-body">The thinking behind the tools, once a week: what platforms reward, what they say they reward, and what it costs the people making the content.</p>
          <form class="sub-form" action="https://jasonnellis.substack.com/subscribe" method="get" target="_blank">
            <input type="email" name="email" placeholder="your@email.com" required class="sub-input" autocomplete="email">
            <button type="submit" class="btn primary sub-btn">Subscribe</button>
          </form>
          <p class="sub-note">Powered by Substack &middot; Unsubscribe anytime</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>

<site-footer></site-footer>

</body>
</html>
